---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const title = "How to Write Your Memoir, Hollywood Style";
const description =
  "Explore a practical book that helps you shape real-life experiences into a clear, engaging memoir.";
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <article>
    <p><a href="/">← Back to home</a></p>

    <h1>How to Write Your Memoir, Hollywood Style</h1>

    <p>
      <img
        src="/images/book-cover.jpg"
        alt="Cover of How to Write Your Memoir, Hollywood Style"
        style="max-width: 300px; width: 100%; height: auto; border-radius: 8px;"
      />
    </p>

    <p>
      A lifetime contains countless memories, but a successful memoir needs more
      than a list of events. It needs focus, structure, emotional movement, and
      a clear sense of what the story means.
    </p>

    <p>
      <em>How to Write Your Memoir, Hollywood Style</em> introduces a practical
      method for using storytelling techniques to turn personal experiences
      into a memoir that feels purposeful and engaging.
    </p>

    <p>
      <a
        href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0GLR2TTDP"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        class="buy-button"
      >
        View the Book on Amazon
      </a>
    </p>

    <h2>Who May Find This Book Useful?</h2>

    <ul>
      <li>people beginning their first memoir</li>
      <li>writers unsure how to organize years of memories</li>
      <li>families documenting personal or family history</li>
      <li>authors who want to make true stories more compelling</li>
      <li>memoir writers looking for a practical writing framework</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Topics Covered in the Book</h2>

    <p>The book helps readers consider questions such as:</p>

    <ul>
      <li>Which part of my life should the memoir focus on?</li>
      <li>What is the central idea or theme of the story?</li>
      <li>How should the events be arranged?</li>
      <li>How can real experiences be written as vivid scenes?</li>
      <li>Which memories belong in the manuscript?</li>
      <li>How can the first idea become a finished book?</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>From Individual Questions to a Complete Process</h2>

    <p>
      The articles on this website explore individual memoir-writing topics.
      The book connects those topics into a broader process that can guide a
      writer from initial planning through drafting and revision.
    </p>

    <h2>Start With the Free Guides</h2>

    <p>
      You can begin with the free articles before deciding whether the complete
      book is right for you.
    </p>

    <p>
      <a href="/articles/">Browse the memoir-writing articles →</a>
    </p>

    <p>
      <a
        href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0GLR2TTDP"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        class="buy-button"
      >
        View the Book on Amazon
      </a>
    </p>
  </article>

  <style>
    .buy-button {
      display: inline-block;
      padding: 0.8rem 1.2rem;
      border-radius: 0.35rem;
      background: #222;
      color: #fff;
      font-weight: 700;
      text-decoration: none;
    }

    .buy-button:hover {
      background: #444;
    }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
